1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:01,066
That hic sound?

2
00:00:01,066 --> 00:00:03,023
It’s your vocal cords slamming shut.

3
00:00:05,250 --> 00:00:08,877
Under your lungs sits the diaphragm — the main muscle you breathe with.

4
00:00:10,750 --> 00:00:14,035
During hiccups, it suddenly spasms and pulls air in fast.

5
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:19,407
A split second later, your vocal cords snap shut — hic!

6
00:00:21,750 --> 00:00:27,211
Common triggers: eating fast or a lot, fizzy drinks, excitement, sudden temperature change.

7
00:00:28,250 --> 00:00:29,516
Most stop on their own.

8
00:00:29,516 --> 00:00:32,325
Holding your breath or sipping cold water may help.

9
00:00:34,250 --> 00:00:39,541
See a doctor if hiccups last over 48 hours, or make it hard to eat, sleep or breathe.
